=95=90 -->
  <div class=3D"section highlight">
    <h2><span class=3D"icon">=E2=9A=A1</span> Short-Term Memory (Working Me=
mory)</h2>
    <p>
      Short-term memory holds everything relevant to the <strong>current ta=
sk or session</strong>.
      It is typically assembled into the context window before each LLM cal=
l, giving the model direct, zero-latency access
      to the current working state.
    </p>

    <ul style=3D"margin-top:0.75rem; line-height:2">
      <li><strong>Conversation history</strong> - all prior user and assist=
ant turns in the session</li>
      <li><strong>Current plan</strong> - active task list, goals, and next=
 steps</li>
      <li><strong>Tool outputs</strong> - API responses, code execution res=
ults, search outputs</li>
      <li><strong>Scratchpad</strong> - intermediate reasoning and chain-of=
-thought steps</li>
      <li><strong>Agent state</strong> - workflow position, loop counters, =
execution flags</li>
      <li><strong>Working context</strong> - retrieved docs or preferences =
injected for this call</li>
    </ul>

    <hr class=3D"divider">

    <h3>Storage - not just RAM</h3>
    <p>
      Short-term memory is <strong>not necessarily stored only in RAM</stro=
ng>.
      It can be persisted to durable storage and still be short-term, as lo=
ng as it belongs to the
      current task or session and is not intended as permanent cross-sessio=
n knowledge.
    </p>
    <div class=3D"grid-2" style=3D"margin-top:0.5rem">
      <div class=3D"card">
        <h3>Common storage backends</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>RAM / in-process dict</li>
          <li>Redis (fast, ephemeral)</li>
          <li>SQL / NoSQL checkpoints</li>
          <li>Workflow state stores (LangGraph, Temporal)</li>
          <li>File-based checkpoints for long-running agents</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"card green">
        <h3>Key characteristic</h3>
        <p>The defining property is <strong>scope</strong>, not storage med=
ium.
           If the data belongs to a current task and will not be consulted =
in future sessions as permanent knowledge,
           it is short-term - regardless of where it lives physically.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

