  <div class=3D"section">
    <h2><span class=3D"icon">=F0=9F=97=9C</span> Managing Large Short-Term =
Memory</h2>
    <p>
      As conversations and agent executions grow, context can exceed the mo=
del's context window.
      These are the common techniques, and most production systems combine =
several of them.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Technique 1: Sliding Window -->
  <div class=3D"pipe-block">
    <div class=3D"pipe-num" style=3D"background:#2a2060;color:var(--accent2=
);">1</div>
    <div class=3D"pipe-body">
      <div class=3D"pipe-title" style=3D"color:var(--accent2)">Sliding Wind=
ow</div>
      <div class=3D"pipe-subtitle">Keep only the most recent N messages.</d=
iv>
      <div class=3D"formula">Keep last 20 messages
Discard older messages</div>
      <div class=3D"pipe-tags">
        <span class=3D"tag">Simplest approach</span>
        <span class=3D"tag blue">O(1) management</span>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"pros-cons">
        <div class=3D"pros">
          <h4>Pros</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Simple to implement</li>
            <li>Fast - no extra LLM calls</li>
            <li>Zero cost overhead</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"cons">
          <h4>Cons</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Important older information is discarded</li>
            <li>No compression - just truncation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Technique 2: Summarization -->
  <div class=3D"pipe-block">
    <div class=3D"pipe-num" style=3D"background:#1a2440;color:var(--accent)=
;">2</div>
    <div class=3D"pipe-body">
      <div class=3D"pipe-title" style=3D"color:var(--accent)">Rolling Summa=
rization</div>
      <div class=3D"pipe-subtitle">Periodically compress older messages int=
o a running summary.</div>
      <div class=3D"formula">100 messages
=E2=86=93
1 summary + recent messages</div>
      <div class=3D"pipe-tags">
        <span class=3D"tag blue">Token reduction</span>
        <span class=3D"tag blue">Preserves gist</span>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"pros-cons">
        <div class=3D"pros">
          <h4>Pros</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Significant token reduction</li>
            <li>Preserves important information</li>
            <li>Maintains conversational continuity</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"cons">
          <h4>Cons</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Summary may lose fine-grained details</li>
            <li>Errors can accumulate over many summarization cycles</li>
            <li>Extra LLM call per summarization</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Technique 3: Message Trimming -->
  <div class=3D"pipe-block">
    <div class=3D"pipe-num" style=3D"background:#0d2e24;color:var(--accent3=
);">3</div>
    <div class=3D"pipe-body">
      <div class=3D"pipe-title" style=3D"color:var(--accent3)">Message Trim=
ming</div>
      <div class=3D"pipe-subtitle">Remove low-value messages that add no si=
gnal.</div>
      <div class=3D"formula">Greetings, "thank you" messages,
repeated confirmations =E2=86=92 remove</div>
      <div class=3D"pipe-tags">
        <span class=3D"tag green">Easy token savings</span>
        <span class=3D"tag green">No LLM cost</span>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"pros-cons">
        <div class=3D"pros">
          <h4>Pros</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Easy wins - often 5=E2=80=9320% token savings</li>
            <li>No additional LLM calls</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"cons">
          <h4>Cons</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Requires heuristics to identify low-value content</li>
            <li>Heuristics can misfire on edge cases</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Technique 4: Semantic Recall -->
  <div class=3D"pipe-block">
    <div class=3D"pipe-num" style=3D"background:#2a2010;color:var(--accent4=
);">4</div>
    <div class=3D"pipe-body">
      <div class=3D"pipe-title" style=3D"color:var(--accent4)">Semantic Rec=
all</div>
      <div class=3D"pipe-subtitle">Move older history into a vector databas=
e - retrieve only what's relevant.</div>
      <div class=3D"formula">Current query: "What project was I working on?=
"
=E2=86=93 Embed query
=E2=86=93 Search vector store of past messages
=E2=86=93 Retrieve: "Last week user discussed educosys.com"
=E2=86=93 Inject into context</div>
      <div class=3D"pipe-tags">
        <span class=3D"tag amber">Vector DB</span>
        <span class=3D"tag amber">Embedding search</span>
        <span class=3D"tag amber">Fuzzy recall</span>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"pros-cons">
        <div class=3D"pros">
          <h4>Pros</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Scales to very large histories</li>
            <li>Only relevant information is injected</li>
            <li>No hard token limit on total history</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"cons">
          <h4>Cons</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Retrieval quality depends on embeddings and search</li>
            <li>May miss relevant context if query is poorly phrased</li>
            <li>Added retrieval latency</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Technique 5: State Extraction -->
  <div class=3D"pipe-block">
    <div class=3D"pipe-num" style=3D"background:#2e1a1a;color:var(--accent5=
);">5</div>
    <div class=3D"pipe-body">
